WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.506
Hi! A train ticket says 18:45. What time is that? Today we'll learn the 24-hour clock.

2
00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:19.722
A day has 24 hours. With the 12-hour clock we write a.m. or p.m. With the 24-hour clock, we don't need to.

3
00:00:19.872 --> 00:00:25.050
For morning times, just write four digits: 9 a.m. is 09:00.

4
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.490
For afternoon and evening times, add 12: 3 p.m. is 3 plus 12, which is 15:00.

5
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:38.586
Remember: noon is 12:00, and midnight is 00:00.

6
00:00:38.736 --> 00:00:48.642
What time is 18:45? It's more than 12, so take away 12: 18 minus 12 is 6. It's 6:45 p.m.

7
00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:53.130
10:20 is less than 12, so it's 10:20 a.m.

8
00:00:53.280 --> 00:01:05.130
Durations work the same way: 13:45 to 14:00 is 15 minutes, 14:00 to 16:00 is 2 hours, then 20 more minutes.

9
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.266
That's 2 hours 35 minutes altogether.

10
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:16.290
Watch out! Some pupils write 4 p.m. as 04:00. That's wrong!

11
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:24.426
04:00 is 4 o'clock in the early morning. For p.m. times, add 12: 4 p.m. is 16:00.

12
00:01:24.576 --> 00:01:30.090
When you finish, ask yourself: is it daytime or night then?

13
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:39.954
Your turn! How do we write 7:30 p.m. on the 24-hour clock? Pause and think.

14
00:01:40.104 --> 00:01:47.106
7 plus 12 is 19, so it's 19:30. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:47.256 --> 00:01:55.626
Another one! What time is 22:15? Pause and think.

16
00:01:55.776 --> 00:02:03.282
22 minus 12 is 10, so it's 10:15 p.m. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:03.432 --> 00:02:13.314
Here's another! How do we write 8:05 a.m. on the 24-hour clock? Pause and think.

18
00:02:13.464 --> 00:02:19.746
Morning times don't change, so it's 08:05. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:19.896 --> 00:02:29.202
Try one more! How do we write midnight on the 24-hour clock? Pause and think.

20
00:02:29.352 --> 00:02:35.874
Midnight is the start of a new day, so it's 00:00. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:36.024 --> 00:02:46.050
Last one! How long is it from 13:45 to 16:20? Pause and think.

22
00:02:46.200 --> 00:03:00.642
13:45 to 14:00 is 15 minutes, then 2 hours to 16:00, then 20 more minutes: 2 hours 35 minutes. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:00.792 --> 00:03:12.642
Remember: on the 24-hour clock, morning times stay the same, and afternoon and evening times add 12. If the hour is more than 12, subtract 12 to get the p.m. time.

24
00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:19.530
Look at a microwave or phone at home. Does it use the 24-hour clock?

